# Corpus source media: ISOs, installer archives and captured video. These are
# untracked working material -- downloads/ alone is 9.8 GB -- and *.png/*.exe
# above did not cover them, so a stray `git add .` in this shared worktree
# would try to commit a 6.7 GB .7z. The notes written beside the payloads are
# worth keeping, which is why this is `downloads/*` with a negation and not a
# blanket `downloads/` (git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored dir).
downloads/*
!downloads/*.md
exports/
*.iso
*.ISO
*.7z
*.mp4

# Static site pages rendered by tools/gen-site-pages.js at deploy time
# (story.html is the one committed output so a local http.server has it).
apps/*.html
articles/*.html
design/*.html
docs/*.html
docs/re-notes/*.html
sitemap.xml

# The DOS corpus report is generated into docs/dos-corpus and is
# committed; the blanket *.png above would otherwise drop its screenshots.
!docs/dos-corpus/shots/*.png

# Private installed DOS payloads; manifests alone are versioned.
test/binaries/toyvm-installed/
